| Arm | Median interface-confidence score (ipTM) | Predicted interface quality (median / max) |
|---|---|---|
| af3 with phosphoserine | 0.917 | 0.75 / 0.81 |
| protenix with phosphoserine | 0.905 | 0.73 / 0.77 |
| boltz-2 with phosphoserine | 0.883 | 0.70 / 0.77 |
| af3 unmodified control | 0.552 | 0.48 / 0.57 |
| openfold3 with phosphoserine | 0.473 | 0.45 / 0.57 |

- With the phosphate, af3, protenix and boltz-2 give confident interfaces.
- The unmodified af3 control is weak, which supports the decision to model the phosphoserine.
- OpenFold3 is also weak. It may not have carried the phosphoserine into its input; nobody has checked that yet, and the next review should.

**Clustering (job 348952):** 12 clusters, split mostly by predictor and variant, each internally very tight (TM ≥ 0.976). The comparison is over the whole complex, so the 233-residue receptor dominates it and it can't tell peptide registers apart. The gates do that job.

